course: dictionary
lesson: 410
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, so context tells you which one the writer means. «Every evening Mum sends off applications» is about job forms, not computers. Ask yourself what meaning fits the sentence, then try it out.
explain: An application can be a written request, like a form asking for a job or a school place. It can also be a computer or phone program, often called an app. Look at the clues around the word to decide which one is meant.
explain: In «Finding a job can take time: 20 job applications with 2 replies is 1 reply in 10», the clues are job, replies and interview. They tell you applications means written requests for jobs. Check by swapping in "requests": it still makes sense.
fact: An application is a written request, like a form asking for a job or a place at school.
fact: An application can also be a computer or phone program, often called an app.
fact: The application of something means putting it to use, like using a rule in maths.
fact: An application can also mean putting cream, paint or glue onto a surface.
fact: Job hunting often means sending many applications and getting few replies: 20 applications with 2 replies is 1 reply in 10.
exercise: «Every evening Mum sits at the laptop sending off applications.» What does application mean here? | A brand of laptop | A meeting at school | A cold drink on a hot day | *A written request for a job
exercise: Ella says, "I need to download this application to my phone." What does application mean? | *A computer or phone program | A meeting to see if you get the job | A written request for a school place | Putting paint on a wall
exercise: Maya's teacher says, "Let's look at the practical applications of fractions." What does application mean? | Sending a letter | Painting a picture | *Using an idea in a real problem | Filling in a form
test: «Grown-ups write a CV, send applications, and go to interviews.» In this sentence, what are applications? | *Written requests for jobs | Sunny days | Computer games | Pieces of cake
test: The teacher says, "Put a thin application of glue on the card." What does application mean? | Using a computer program | A written request for a job | *Putting glue onto a surface | A meeting for a job
exam: Mum fills in an application form for a job in Toronto. Which meaning of application fits best? | Putting glue on a surface | *A written request for something | A computer program | Using a rule in maths
